## Consequences

(+) `cloud-itonami-isic-5811` now has a real, tested implementation
matching the shape of every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor, replacing a
`:spec` placeholder pointing at a repo that never existed.

(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"5811\"` entry promoted to
`:maturity :implemented`.

(+) This actor is a second concrete example (after `cloud-itonami-isic-
873`) of Wave 4's person-facing-service safety guardrail applied to a
different sensitive-decision axis: instead of clinical/care-authority
exclusions, this actor structurally excludes editorial-content-decision,
legal-risk-clearance, and rights/licensing-grant authority, all folded
into one unconditional scope-exclusion check that never trusts the
advisor's own framing of its intent.

(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer, not a real publishing-operations
system. Editorial decisions, legal clearance, and rights/licensing
grants remain human-/institution-controlled via external channels.

(-) No integration with real publishing-house systems (manuscript
management, print-run scheduling, ISBN registries, rights/licensing
databases, distribution partner APIs) -- this is a standalone
coordinator blueprint, matching every prior sibling actor's own stated
